    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d215">

                <pb facs="0206" n="200" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg200"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Prince Cantacuzene.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-05-12"><hi rendition="#italic">May 12,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 4th instant, and to express to you the gratification with
                    which this Government accepts your declaration that the Imperial Government is
                    prepared to negotiate and sign with the United States, England, and Japan a
                    treaty in virtue of which the principles and regulations of the Paris Tribunal
                    of Arbitration shall be applicable, indifferently, to all the waters of the
                    Pacific Ocean north of the thirty-fifth parallel of north latitude.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
